  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Here's how the $12.00 works out:\n\n- Your order subtotal was $50.00 (2 phos at $15 each, spring rolls at $7, banh mi at $13).\n- The WELCOME10 promo took $10.00 off that subtotal.\n- The missing pho is $15.00 of the $50.00, or 30%. Its share of the discount is 30% of $10.00, which is $3.00.\n- Card refund: $15.00 \u2212 $3.00 = **$12.00**.\n- The $3.00 discount share comes back to you as account credit.\n\nYou get the full $15.00 value back: $12.00 on your card and $3.00 in credit. I'll process both now.\n\nI've processed both for the missing pho:\n\n- **$12.00 refund** to your Visa ending 4242. It should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n- **$3.00 account credit**, which is already in your balance and can be used on a future order.\n\nI'm sorry again for the missing pho. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so $12 on the card plus $3 in credit adds up to the $15 I paid for that pho, so that works. I didn't know about the promo part though. I used a welcome code when I signed up, but I don't remember how much it was for. Should I be worried the credit isn't cash?\n\nAnyway, thanks for sorting it out. I'll see the card refund in a few days."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "No need to worry. The $3.00 credit is your share of the WELCOME10 discount, which was $10.00 off your order. A promo discount is never paid out as cash, so getting that part back as credit is the standard way to handle it. You haven't lost any value. The credit is in your account and you can apply it to a future Forkful order.\n\nThe $12.00 refund should reach your card in 3\u20135 business days. Enjoy the rest of your evening, Owen!"
  }
